@@ -3,3 +3,28 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document: unknown, pointer: string): unknown`, exported from `src/index.ts`,
+locates a value using an [RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901.html).
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from './src/index.js';
+
+const document = { users: [{ name: 'Ada' }], 'a/b': true };
+resolvePointer(document, '/users/0/name'); // 'Ada'
+resolvePointer(document, '/a~1b');         // true
+resolvePointer(document, '');             // document itself
+```
+
+Pass a parsed JSON value and a decoded pointer string. Tokens use `~0` for `~` and `~1` for `/`.
+An empty token selects an empty object key. Array tokens must be zero-based decimal indices without
+leading zeroes; `-` does not resolve to an element. Object keys are compared exactly, without Unicode
+normalization. URI fragments such as `#/users/0` are not accepted, and percent escapes are not decoded.
+
+Malformed pointers and missing values throw an `Error`, including traversal through a primitive or
+an inherited property. Values are returned by reference without modifying the document. The function
+assumes its document is already a JSON value; it does not parse or validate the entire document.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` on Node.js 22.18 or later (with built-in TypeScript support).
