+---
+id: dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-token-resolution
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use strict RFC 6901 token resolution"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need one shared way to locate values in JSON documents, and follow-on features will rely on
+its failure semantics.
+
+## Decision
+
+Interpret pointers strictly according to RFC 6901: the empty string addresses the whole document;
+all non-empty pointers start with `/`; reference tokens unescape `~1` to `/` and `~0` to `~`; arrays
+accept only canonical non-negative decimal indices; and missing members, invalid escapes, invalid
+indices, or attempts to traverse a primitive throw an error.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The resolver has predictable standards-based behavior and does not silently accept malformed input
+or JavaScript-specific property access.
